  "vendor_website": "proser.com.ar",
  "description": "Gas volume corrector: pressure, temperature, corrected and uncorrected flow and volumes, gas composition, alarm limits and alarm states, with remote writing of clock, chromatography and alarm settings",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-15",
  "source": "PROSER UCV-117 Manual de usuario",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "UCV-117 Manual de usuario",
      "url": "https://www.proser.com.ar/assets/downloads/manuales/Manual%20UCV-117-REV%20F.pdf",
      "note": "Section 4.1, Modbus memory map",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "b44446340711113fd2146575f503e8a954fbef995b1a630c0371b403dfe25a95"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The device has two floating-point layouts: Modicon (16-bit registers, each float over two registers from 7001) and Enron (one numbered 32-bit register per value, 7001 to 7121). This map follows the Modicon layout, the factory type; in the Enron layout the same variables are at the manual's 32-bit numbers.",
    "Coils start at address 0 (function 01).",
    "Writing: put the new values in the writable table, write the security code (the sum of the ASCII codes of the 8-character access key, for example 420 for 12345678) in 7157, then the write code in 7155, and check 7157 for the result. Needs firmware 2.08 or later, which also adds the extended map (gas composition, alarm limits, serial number).",
    "The hourly and daily history (up to 120 days) is stored in flash and is not described here.",
    "RS-232 only, Modbus ASCII or RTU, 300 to 9600 bps, address 1 to 244; factory RTU 9600 8N1 address 18, and the port is switched off at the factory to save battery. Word order of the floats is not stated; big-endian assumed.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual (Spanish); not tested on a device."
  ],
